Title: Zotero tests fail intermittently with 401 under parallel gate runs
Created: 2026-10-27
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-27T11:19Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
Raid 2026-10-27, author ruling (ticket, from the raid's time-saving review). Observed twice on padme:
the #1736 gate's first `pytest-guard` run failed two tests in `tests/test_zotero_import.py` with HTTP 401
from the local Zotero API (each passed 3 of 3 alone), and the #1746 ticket-only gate failed
`pytest-guard` once while an isolated `make check-tests` on the same tree passed (2430 passed). The
gate keeps no per-test log, so the second failing test is not identified. Cause not established;
parallel runs sharing the local API key or server is one hypothesis. Each occurrence costs a full
re-record (about 75-90 s) and can block a merge.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Reproduce: the failing test identified, with the condition that triggers the 401 (or the
      hypothesis refuted with the run that refutes it).
- [ ] The zotero tests cannot fail from another concurrent run: isolated credentials/server or a
      stub, or moved to a tier the gate does not run, with the reason stated.
- [ ] `merge-gate.py run` keeps the failing test names of a failed check (one line each) so the next
      flake is named, not guessed.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
tests/test_zotero_import.py, scripts/merge-gate.py, pytest.ini

## Raid annotation (Imagine+Plan, 2026-10-27, wave 4)
- **Verdict: GO.** Cause found by reading, to be confirmed by the reproduction below (cause not yet established by experiment).
- **Likely cause.** `tests/test_zotero_import.py` autouse `zotero_down` (l.59-68) makes every test point at a "closed" port via `free_port()` (tests/zotero_live.py l.120): it binds port 0, reads the number and closes the socket. The port is free only until some other process takes it. The live fixture in the same file (`ZoteroClient`, zotero_live.py l.311, also `free_port()`) starts a real throwaway Zotero on such a port, with a key store that trusts only its own key. A concurrent gate run (other xdist workers or another worktree's gate) can bind the released port first; the "down" test then reaches a live Zotero with an empty key file and gets 401 instead of connection refused. Matches: 401 not connection error, passes alone 3/3, fails under parallel gates, a different test each time. Hypothesis, not yet shown.
- **Reproduction plan.** (1) Loop `free_port()` collisions: from two processes run 2000 iterations each of bind/close/record and count shared ports (cheap, shows the window is real on a 64-CPU padme with xdist). (2) End to end: `python3 -m pytest tests/test_zotero_import.py -n 16 -p no:cacheprovider` in 3 concurrent shells of a loop, 20 rounds, with `-rf` kept to name failures (`pytest_workers.py` gives `-n` count; 64 CPUs here). (3) Positive control: in a test run, start a keyed server on the port a test was given and confirm the 401 text. Null results at low parallelism prove nothing.
- **Simplest isolation.** Hold the port instead of releasing it: `zotero_down` keeps a bound, never-listening socket open for the test (yield the socket, close at teardown), so nobody can bind it and a connect is refused. No new moving parts. Same hold for the `ZoteroClient` port is not possible (Zotero binds it), so retry-on-bind-failure there, or run integration tests off the gate (they carry `@pytest.mark.integration` already but `check-tests` runs everything: Makefile l.58). Choose the hold first; move integration out of `check-tests` only if the hold does not remove it.
- **merge-gate.py and failing test names.** `run_checks` (l.450) runs `subprocess.run(item["argv"], cwd=cwd)` with output uninspected. Capture stdout+stderr, echo it unchanged to stderr, and on failure scan for pytest `^FAILED <nodeid>` summary lines (default `-rf`), recording them. Constraint: `red_report` (1244, `zip(config["checks"], results)`) assumes one result line per check; extra `failed-test` lines break that zip. Fix in the same PR: `red_report` matches by name prefix, or the names ride in the same line after the verdict. Pick the former to honour "one line each".
- **Function overlap with 1245.** 1254 edits `run_checks` only (plus `red_report` match). 1245 edits `load_config`, `effective`, `accepted_scopes`, `cmd_run`, `cmd_plan`, the docstring; it passes a filtered config into `run_checks`, interface unchanged. Disjoint hunks; 1251 also edits `red_report` and `run_after`: take 1254's `red_report` change first or merge together.
- **Risk.** Medium: the cause may be elsewhere (a shared `~/.config/keys` path is excluded by the fixture setting `ZOTERO_LOCAL_KEY_FILE`); the reproduction decides before the fix.
